libqjs attaches each weak native reference (js_ref_t at count 0, including every
jstl js_persistent_t::reset() in rocksdb-native and udx-native) as a symbol
property [Symbol("__native_reference")] -> External(js_finalizer_t) on the
referenced JS object with flags = 0 (non-configurable), then calls
JS_DeleteProperty(..., 0) in js__clear_weak_reference. QuickJS delete_property
returns FALSE (0) on non-configurable properties, which satisfies assert(err >= 0)
while leaving the Symbol, External object, 64-byte js_finalizer_t, and growing
JSShape slot pinned on long-lived objects (such as RocksDB's State and onread
callback) forever (~4 KB leaked per RocksDB read/write, swelling PearTube.app to
2+ GB). Define the weak-reference property with JS_PROP_CONFIGURABLE so
js__clear_weak_reference actually deletes it, frees the External and finalizer on
the spot, and lets QuickJS compact the object's shape. Apply in libqjs, after
libqjs-deferred-release.patch.

diff --git a/src/js.c b/src/js.c
--- a/src/js.c
+++ b/src/js.c
@@ -2127,7 +2127,7 @@ js__set_weak_reference(js_env_t *env, js_ref_t *reference) {
 
     JSAtom atom = JS_ValueToAtom(env->context, reference->symbol);
 
-    err = JS_DefinePropertyValue(env->context, reference->value, atom, external, 0);
+    err = JS_DefinePropertyValue(env->context, reference->value, atom, external, JS_PROP_CONFIGURABLE);
     assert(err >= 0);
 
     JS_FreeAtom(env->context, atom);
